> Is there any rule for how long the binding lasts, or is it left to context?

The rule is that bindings last through all logically connected bridi.
By extension, an isolated da-series after the next bare ".i" (or "ni'o")
can be assumed bound.  To override this assumption, use "da'o" to clear
pro-sumti/pro-bridi assignments.

